# Zoom Participant Factory

## /participant
This directory contains a Python script that connects to a Zoom meeting using Selenium. It also contains a Dockerfile such that this script can be run inside a container.

### Usage
```shell

export ZOOM_DISPLAY_NAME=participantA
export ZOOM_MEETING_ID=
export ZOOM_MEETING_PASSCODE=
export ZOOM_SESSION_LENGTH_SECONDS=30

# manually
python3 participant.py

# Docker
docker build . -t participant:latest && \
docker run --rm -it \
    --env ZOOM_DISPLAY_NAME=$ZOOM_DISPLAY_NAME \
    --env ZOOM_MEETING_ID=$ZOOM_MEETING_ID \
    --env ZOOM_MEETING_PASSCODE=$ZOOM_MEETING_PASSCODE \
    --env ZOOM_SESSION_LENGTH_SECONDS=$ZOOM_SESSION_LENGTH_SECONDS \
    participant:latest
```
